Subject: [PATCH 4/5] test(acceptance): each album's images and place, each
 folder's path, name and images
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tests/c1_acceptance.py checked album image counts and the folder tree's
parents. The owner's acceptance asks for the photos, paths, ratings and the
folder structure to be right, so it now also checks, against the same
independent reading of a byte copy:

- every album holds the same images as in Capture One (images.list with
  that collection), not only the same number;
- every album sits where it does in Capture One: at the top level, or in
  its album group (an album inside a group, as Capture One's "Trips" >
  "测试相册");
- every folder's path is the independent resolution, its name is the
  folder's own name (non-ASCII included; a volume root is named by its
  path), and it holds the images whose location it is.

Gate: on Linux against the synthetic catalog and session, 36 passed,
0 failed. Against copies of the Capture One 16.6.4 for Windows test
catalog and session read on Linux (where ZMACROOT is empty, so paths are
not resolvable), every check that does not depend on the platform's root
passes; with the oracle in Windows mode the folder tree matches spklib's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
